## PackageGuard Android App Layout

- **App entry**: [`app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/PackageGuardApp.kt`](mdc:app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/PackageGuardApp.kt)
- **DI**:
  - Hilt network module: [`app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/di/NetworkModule.kt`](mdc:app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/di/NetworkModule.kt)
- **Networking**:
  - Retrofit interface: [`app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/data/remote/api/PackageGuardApi.kt`](mdc:app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/data/remote/api/PackageGuardApi.kt)
  - DTOs: [`app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/data/remote/dto`](mdc:app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/data/remote/dto)
- **Presentation (MVVM)**:
  - Splash: [`app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/presentation/splash`](mdc:app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/presentation/splash)
  - Auth: [`app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/presentation/auth`](mdc:app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/presentation/auth)
  - Seller dashboard: [`app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/presentation/seller`](mdc:app/src/main/java/io/packageguard/app/presentation/seller)

The Android client is intentionally **thin**: it should only orchestrate UI, camera, and uploads, while all business logic and validation stay on the backend.

